## Go Karting

Indoor go kart racing at AeroSports Scarborough features two tracks: a main track designed for taller riders and a Mini Track suitable for younger children. Participants can enjoy up to ten laps per race on electric karts.

- **Age/Height Requirements:** Main Track requires participants to be fifty-two inches tall. The Mini Track is for those who are thirty-six inches tall. Closed-toed shoes are required.
- **Included in Jump Pass:** No
- **Pricing:** This attraction requires a separate ticket or can be added as an add-on. For pricing details, refer to the Go Karting sheet.

[6] (source: voice_call_scripts.md)
## Go-Kart Overview

At AeroSports Scarborough, we have two go-kart tracks available. The main track is suitable for riders who are fifty-four inches or taller and costs nineteen dollars and ninety cents per standalone race. If you already possess a jump pass, the add-on cost is nine dollars and ninety cents. Our mini track accommodates riders who are thirty-six inches or taller and charges nine dollars and ninety cents for a standalone race or four dollars and ninety cents as an add-on if you have a jump pass. Each race allows up to ten laps. Remember that closed-toed shoes are required for go-karting.

[7] (source: birthday_parties.md)
## Available Add-Ons

Birthday party add-ons available at AeroSports Scarborough include large pizzas—cheese, pepperoni, halal pepperoni, vegetarian, or Hawaiian—for twenty-five dollars each. Juice boxes (ten boxes) are priced at thirty dollars, soft drink cans (ten cans) cost twenty dollars, and physical birthday invitations are available for seventy-five cents each. An outside food fee of fifty dollars is waived for the Ultimate Party. A go kart race add-on costs nine dollars and ninety cents per person but is already included in the Ultimate Party package. A late ordering fee within twenty-four hours amounts to twenty dollars.


